<!-- spacerace.xml -->
<!-- XML Game Engine -->
<!-- author: beefviper -->
<!-- date: Sept 30, 2026 -->

<!--
  Space Race (1973): two rockets start at the bottom and fly up through lanes of
  debris drifting sideways. A hit sends a rocket back to the bottom; getting off
  the top of the screen scores a point and sends it back for another go. The
  original played to a two minute clock; this plays to two points, to be quick.

  It uses nothing that was not already in the language: held move.* for the
  rockets, wrap() and hand-spaced objects for the debris (a lane of objects
  `size` wide repeats every window width plus `size`), reset() when a rocket is
  hit, inc() and reset() on the top edge, and a variable condition to end it.
-->

<game xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../assets/xmlgameengine.xsd">
